{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftExtras\/documentation\/SwiftExtras","doc:\/\/SwiftExtras\/documentation\/SwiftExtras\/Swift","doc:\/\/SwiftExtras\/documentation\/SwiftExtras\/Swift\/String"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftExtras\/documentation\/SwiftExtras\/Swift\/String\/sdbmhash"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sdbmhash","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This algorithm was created for sdbm (a public-domain reimplementation of ndbm) database library."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it was found to do well in scrambling bits, causing better distribution of the keys and fewer splits."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it also happens to be a good general hashing function with good distribution."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the actual function is hash(i) = hash(i - 1) * 65599 + str[i];"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"what is included below is the faster version used in gawk."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[there is even a faster, duff-device version] the magic prime constant 65599 (2^6 + 2^16 - 1)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was picked out of thin air while experimenting with many different constants."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this is one of the algorithms used in berkeley db (see sleepycat) and elsewhere."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"abstract"